<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt</h1><p class="st-meta">1567 CE – 1806 CE · capital Darmstadt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The youngest of the Hessian landgraviates, ruled from Darmstadt, which grew into the Grand Duchy of Hesse.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The 1567 division of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/landgraviate-of-hesse">Landgraviate of Hesse</a> gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-i-landgrave-of-hesse-darmstadt">George I</a>, youngest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-i-landgrave-of-hesse">Philip the Magnanimous</a>, the Upper <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-katzenelnbogen">County of Katzenelnbogen</a>, about an eighth of the land, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> as capital. Shares of Hesse-Rheinfels in 1583 and of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a> in 1604 enlarged it.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The landgraves remained Lutheran and loyal to the emperor, unlike Calvinist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a>. Louis V founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-giessen">University of Giessen</a> in 1607, and in 1622 a cadet line was established as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/landgraviate-of-hesse-homburg">Landgraviate of Hesse-Homburg</a>. The landgraves inherited the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-hanau-lichtenberg">County of Hanau-Lichtenberg</a> in 1736, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caroline-of-zweibrucken">Landgravine Caroline</a> made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> court a meeting place for writers, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-wolfgang-von-goethe">Goethe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-gottfried-herder">Herder</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-grand-duke-of-hesse">Landgrave Louis X</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> in 1806 and became Grand Duke Louis I of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Grand Duchy of Hesse</a>, which lasted until 1918.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/landgraviate-of-hesse-darmstadt.jpg" alt="Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt" width="320" height="280"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hesse-Darmstadt_Regiment_during_the_Seven_Years_War_(1756-1763).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1567 CE – 1806 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Darmstadt</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>George I, Louis V, Louis X</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hessen-Darmstadt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1686&amp;focus=landgraviate-of-hesse-darmstadt" aria-label="Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4878 442 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5198 698L5183 654M5198 698L5215 656M5198 698L5229 694M5198 698L5198 698M5198 698L5197 688M5198 698L5173 729M5198 698L5192 705M5198 698L5211 717M5198 698L5200 685"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5183 654h0M5215 656h0M5229 694h0M5198 698h0M5197 688h0M5173 729h0M5192 705h0M5211 717h0M5200 685h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5198 698h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5198 698h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Darmstadt. <a href="/atlas?year=1686&amp;focus=landgraviate-of-hesse-darmstadt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
